      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "80a57c8c97c7-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "Which Article of the Constitution explains that the executive power of every state shall be so exercised as not to impede or prejudice the exercise of the executive power of the Union, and the executive power of the union shall extend to the giving of such directions to a state as may appear to the Government of India to be necessary for that purpose? Options: &#2360;&#2306;&#2357;&#2367;&#2343;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2359;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2358;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2328; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2358;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2348;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366; &#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2361; &#2344; &#2361;&#2379;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2328; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2358;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2320;&#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368; &#2332;&#2379; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2360;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;? &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which Article of the Constitution explains that the executive power of every state shall be so exercised as not to impede or prejudice the exercise of the executive power of the Union, and the executive power of the union shall extend to the giving of such directions to a state as may appear to the Government of India to be necessary for that purpose?</p><p>Options:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2306;&#2357;&#2367;&#2343;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2359;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2358;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2328; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2358;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2348;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366; &#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2361; &#2344; &#2361;&#2379;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2328; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2358;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2320;&#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368; &#2332;&#2379; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2360;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;?</p><p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Article 261 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 261",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Article 261</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 261</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Article 247 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 247",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Article 247</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 247</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Article 257 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 257",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Article 257</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 257</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Article 123 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 123",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Article 123</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 123</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>&#183; <b>Article 257</b> of the Indian Constitution ensures that the <b>executive power</b> of a state does not interfere with the <b>executive power</b> of the Union.</p><p>&#183; It allows the Union to issue directions to states to ensure coordination and compliance with national interests.</p><p>Incorrect options:</p><p>&#183; <b>Article 261</b> deals with the recognition of public acts, records, and judicial proceedings.</p><p>&#183; <b>Article 247</b> provides for the power of Parliament to establish certain additional courts.</p><p>&#183; <b>Article 123</b> relates to the President's power to promulgate ordinances.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
