        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Article 177 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 177",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Article 177</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 177</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Article 167 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 167",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Article 167</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 167</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Article 164 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 164",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Article 164</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 164</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Article 166 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 166",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Article 166</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; 166</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Article 166 of the Indian Constitution specifically deals with the conduct of business of the Government of a state.</p><p>Key Points:</p><p>&#183; Provides rules for transaction of government business</p><p>&#183; Defines how state government business should be conducted</p><p>&#183; Specifies the Governor's role in state administration</p><p>&#183; Ensures systematic and orderly functioning of state government</p><p>&#183; Part of the constitutional provisions governing state executive</p><p>&#183; Helps maintain transparency in governmental processes</p><p>&#183; Supports the principle of responsible governance</p>",
